From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/sd/sdcard: Let a card be inserted into an empty slot

Since commit a362b19a39e4 ("hw/sd/sdcard: Fix size check for backing
block image"), an SD card realized with a drive that holds no medium
takes no permissions on the drive and registers no callbacks with it.
The drive is then not removable, so a board's empty slot can no longer
take a card: "change" and "blockdev-change-medium" fail with "Device
'sd0' is not removable". Such is the slot of every board that sets
auto_create_sdcard, until -drive if=sd fills it.

Check the size of the medium when there is one, as that commit does,
but take the permissions and register the callbacks for every drive
again.

Fixes: a362b19a39e4 ("hw/sd/sdcard: Fix size check for backing block image")
---
 hw/sd/sd.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/sd/sd.c b/hw/sd/sd.c
index a30c541..30b1bf8 100644
--- a/hw/sd/sd.c
+++ b/hw/sd/sd.c
@@ -3145,7 +3145,8 @@ static void sd_realize(DeviceState *dev, Error **errp)
             error_setg(errp, "eMMC image smaller than boot partitions");
             return;
         }
-
+    }
+    if (sd->blk) {
         ret = blk_set_perm(sd->blk, BLK_PERM_CONSISTENT_READ | BLK_PERM_WRITE,
                            BLK_PERM_ALL, errp);
         if (ret < 0) {
